The Apollo Hospitals Patient Billing and Insurance Claims Database project creates a unified SQL environment for reviewing the hospital revenue cycle—from patient visits and delivered services to invoices, payments, insurance claims, and claim-status updates. It addresses problems such as unbilled services, rejected or overdue claims, duplicate claim references, missing claim submissions, mismatched amounts, and outstanding invoices.
The solution uses SQLite in Google Colab, supported by Python for API consumption, data validation, loading, and visualization. It includes ten connected core tables, three operational tables, five API activities, and thirteen SQL analyses covering reconciliation, outstanding balances, insurer rejection rates, trends, and follow-up priorities. It also demonstrates COMMIT and ROLLBACK controls and defines scheduled reporting, cron configurations, Git collaboration, and safe database-change workflows.
Using reproducible simulated data, the notebook’s saved completion dashboard shows 26 of 26 activities passed, with no saved error outputs. The intended benefit is to help billing, claims, and finance teams identify revenue gaps and prioritize follow-up through consistent, traceable SQL reports. Scheduling is designed and validated; permanent automated execution requires a scheduler outside Colab.
